  "A small cross-shaped Classical library of 1907, which its National Register nomination likens to a little Palladian villa, of beige pressed brick with light sandstone trim, paired brick pilasters and Public Library lettered across the front. A local history calls it the town's first Classical building. It was the Bannock County Historical Society's museum when listed in 1973, and is now part of the Marshall Public Library, joined to a much larger new building by an atrium. Wikipedia gives the address as 105 South Garfield; the library gives 113.",
