  "A Beaux-Arts library by Watkins, Birch & Wright of Provo, dedicated on March 27, 1915, with pilasters on every side and a basement faced with terra cotta tiles. Its yellow brick has been painted white. A 2008 renovation added an elevator; a planned west addition was never built for lack of money. It is still the Ephraim Public Library. On the National Register since 1984.",
