  "Finished in 1916 between the St. George Tabernacle and the Woodward School, with $8,000 from Carnegie and $4,000 from the city, it became the Washington County Library in 1919. It was torn down in October 1981 after a new county library was built, and the block is now Town Square Park. The old library's doors survive as the entrance to the Special Collections room of the present county library.",
